+# Threshold Feature Implementation Summary
+
+## Feature Overview
+Added `--threshold` option to `frai eval` command to fail CI pipelines when evaluation metrics fall below specified minimums.
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### Files Changed
+
+#### 1. **frai-core/src/eval/index.js**
+- Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter
+- Computes pass/fail for each threshold (passes if score >= min, fails if score is null)
+- Adds `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array to report only when thresholds are provided
+
+#### 2. **frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js**
+- Updated `toMarkdown()` to include a "## Thresholds" section
+- Shows PASS/FAIL status for each threshold with metric name, min value, and actual score
+
+#### 3. **frai-cli/src/index.ts**
+- Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` interface
+- Added `parseThresholds()` function to parse and validate `<metric>=<number>` format
+- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to parse, validate, and apply thresholds
+- Added `--threshold` CLI option (can be given multiple times)
+- Exit code 2 for malformed thresholds or unknown metrics
+- Exit code 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass or no thresholds given
+
+#### 4. **frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js**
+- Added 5 comprehensive tests for threshold functionality
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### No thresholds (existing behavior - unchanged)
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references references.json
+# Exit code: 0 (always, since no thresholds)
+# Report: no 'passed' or 'thresholds' fields
+```
+
+### Single passing threshold
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references references.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9
+# Exit code: 0 (exact_match score >= 0.9)
+# Report JSON: { passed: true, thresholds: [{ metric: "exact_match", min: 0.9, score: X, passed: true }] }
+```
+
+### Single failing threshold
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references references.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.99
+# Exit code: 1 (exact_match score < 0.99)
+# Report JSON: { passed: false, thresholds: [{ metric: "exact_match", min: 0.99, score: X, passed: false }] }
+```
+
+### Multiple thresholds
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references references.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.8 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.9 \
+  --threshold length_variance=0.7
+# Exit code: 0 if all pass, 1 if any fail
+# Report JSON: includes all threshold results
+```
+
+### Markdown report with thresholds
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references references.json \
+  --format markdown \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9
+# Markdown includes:
+# ## Thresholds
+# - **exact_match:** PASS (min: 0.9, score: 0.95)
+```
+
+### Error handling
+```bash
+# Malformed threshold format
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold "invalid"
+# Exit code: 2
+# Error: Malformed threshold: "invalid" (expected format: <metric>=<number>)
+
+# Unknown metric
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold unknown_metric=0.5
+# Exit code: 2
+# Error: Unknown metric: "unknown_metric" (valid metrics: exact_match, toxicity, length_variance)
+
+# Out-of-range value
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=1.5
+# Exit code: 2
+# Error: Invalid threshold value for metric "exact_match": 1.5 (must be between 0 and 1)
+```
+
+## Validation Rules
+
+- Threshold format: `<metric>=<number>`
+- Metric name: must match one of the available metrics
+- Minimum value: must be between 0 and 1 (inclusive)
+- Available metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+- Custom metrics: supported via SDK by passing thresholds object to `generateReport()`
+
+## Test Results
+
+All new tests passing:
+- ✓ applies thresholds and marks them as passed
+- ✓ marks thresholds as failed when score is below minimum
+- ✓ fails threshold when metric has no score
+- ✓ does not include threshold data when no thresholds provided
+- ✓ includes thresholds in markdown report
+
+## SDK Usage
+
+For SDK users, the feature is available via `frai-core`:
+
+```javascript
+import { generateReport } from 'frai-core';
+
+const report = generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: '/path/to/outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: '/path/to/references.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95,
+    length_variance: 0.8
+  }
+});
+
+// Check if thresholds passed
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+Works with custom metrics:
+```javascript
+const customMetric = {
+  id: 'custom_metric',
+  evaluate: (outputs, references) => ({
+    id: 'custom_metric',
+    score: calculateScore(outputs, references),
+    // ... other fields
+  })
+};
+
+const evaluations = runEvaluations({
+  outputs,
+  references,
+  metrics: [customMetric, ...DEFAULT_METRICS]
+});
+
+const report = generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  thresholds: { custom_metric: 0.85 }  // Works with custom metrics
+});
+```
